Amazon Linux 2023 Ansible Setup — Step-by-Step Guide 🚀
I recently completed Ansible setup on Amazon Linux 2023 with 1 Master and 4 Slave servers. Here’s how you can do it:

 1️⃣ Launch 1 Master & 4 Slave instances
 2️⃣ On Master: Install Python3, pip3, and Ansible using dnf
 3️⃣ Set root user password and enable SSH password authentication
 4️⃣ Repeat password setup and SSH configuration on Slave servers
 5️⃣ Generate SSH key on Master and copy the public key to Slaves for pass wordless login
 6️⃣ Create Ansible configuration file /etc/ansible/ansible.cfg and hosts inventory /etc/ansible/hosts
 7️⃣ Test connectivity with ansible all -m ping

🚀 What is Ansible? 🚀
Ansible is an open-source automation tool that helps you automate IT tasks without manual intervention. Using simple YAML scripts called playbooks, you can automate:
Server configuration
Software installation
Application deployment
Continuous delivery pipelines
Complex orchestration workflows
In simple terms, Ansible helps you manage and automate your infrastructure quickly, reliably, and at scale.

🔧 Why this setup is useful:
✅ Centralized management: Manage multiple servers from a single control node
✅ Automation: Automate repetitive tasks like updates, installs, and configurations
✅ Scalability: Easily add or remove servers from your infrastructure
✅ Consistency: Ensure uniform configuration across all servers
✅ Speed: Deploy changes faster and reduce human error

💡 Bonus tip: Use the dnf package manager for installing Ansible and Python pip on Amazon Linux 2023!
